Reproduced on `claude/fresh-bug-repro-sweep-gdleyn` (e8001dc), debug build (`cargo build`), Linux, tmux 3.4 120x34, config `{ "editor": { "restore_previous_session": false } }` with `HOME` pointed at an empty temp dir and `--no-restore --no-upgrade-check`.

Current behaviour: **`.h` is always C, with no content or project-layout influence.** Same bytes in `widget.h` and `widget.hpp`; only the extension differs.

Steps:

1. Write this as `widget.h`, and an identical copy as `widget.hpp`:

```cpp
#pragma once
#include <string>
namespace ui {
class Widget {
public:
    explicit Widget(const std::string& name) : name_(name) {}
    virtual ~Widget() = default;
    template <typename T>
    T clamp(T v, T lo, T hi) const { return v < lo ? lo : (v > hi ? hi : v); }
private:
    std::string name_;
};
}  // namespace ui
```

2. `fresh --config <cfg> --no-restore --no-upgrade-check widget.h`
3. Read the language cell in the status bar, and the colour capture of the body rows.
4. Repeat with `widget.hpp`.

Observed — status bar, `.h`:

```
 Trusted  Local  Ln 1, Col 1     Opened widget.h                             LF  ASCII  C   LSP (off)   Palette: Ctrl+P
```

and `.hpp`:

```
 Trusted  Local  Ln 1, Col 1     Opened widget.hpp                         LF  ASCII  C++   LSP (off)   Palette: Ctrl+P
```

The highlighting follows. `tmux capture-pane -e`, keyword colour is SGR `38;5;51`. For `widget.h`, `namespace`, `class`, `public`, `explicit`, `virtual`, `template`, `typename` all come out in plain foreground `38;5;231` — only the C-and-C++ common tokens (`#pragma`, `const`, `default`, `return`) are keyworded:

```
 3 │ [38;5;231mnamespace ui [38;5;6m{
 4 │ [38;5;231mclass Widget [38;5;2m{
 5 │ [38;5;231mpublic[38;5;251m:
 6 │ [38;5;231m    explicit [38;5;226mWidget[38;5;3m([38;5;51mconst[38;5;226m std:[38;5;231m:[38;5;226mstring[38;5;231m&[38;5;226m name...
```

The same bytes as `widget.hpp`:

```
 3 │ [38;5;51mnamespace[38;5;231m ui [38;5;6m{
 4 │ [38;5;51mclass[38;5;231m [38;5;207mWidget[38;5;231m [38;5;2m{
 5 │ [38;5;51mpublic[38;5;251m:
 6 │ [38;5;231m    [38;5;51mexplicit[38;5;231m [38;5;226mWidget[38;5;3m([38;5;51mconst[38;5;231m std[38;5;251m::[38;5;231mstring& name...
```

Note also `std::string` on line 6: `.hpp` scopes `::` as an operator, `.h` splits it as `std:` + `:`.

## Where the mapping lives

Two tables, both saying `h` → C:

* `crates/fresh-editor/src/config.rs:4351` — the built-in default config: `languages.c.extensions = ["c", "h"]`. This is the one detection actually consults; `languages.cpp` lists `cpp, hpp, cc, hh, cxx, hxx` and not `h`.
* `crates/fresh-languages/src/lib.rs:487` — `Language::extensions()`, the tree-sitter catalogue: `Self::C => &["c", "h"]`, `Self::Cpp => &["cpp", "hpp", "cc", "hh", "cxx", "hxx", "cppm", "ixx"]`. `Language::from_path` (`lib.rs:195`) is derived from it by linear scan, and `C` precedes `Cpp` in `all()`.

## A C++ promotion heuristic already exists — but it does not reach highlighting

`crates/fresh-editor/src/services/lsp/manager.rs:1944` (`detect_language`) already promotes `.h` to `cpp` when the surrounding tree "smells like C++" — sibling C++ sources or an ancestor `compile_commands.json` (`manager.rs:1950`-`1961`, `header_in_cpp_tree`, with tests at `manager.rs:2601`+).

It has no effect on what you see. Measured: a directory containing only `widget.h` and a sibling `widget.cpp` — the decisive signal that heuristic looks for — still opens the header as C:

```
 Trusted  Local  Ln 1, Col 1     Opened widget.h                             LF  ASCII  C   LSP (off)   Palette: Ctrl+P
```

The reason is in `crates/fresh-editor/src/primitives/detected_language.rs`. `from_path_with_fallback` computes `config_lang_id` from that promoting `detect_language` (`detected_language.rs:86`), but `override_name` (`:87`-`:92`) applies it to `d.name` **only** — the config/LSP id. The `highlighter` and `ts_language` come from `registry.find_by_path(path, first_line)` at `detected_language.rs:94`, which resolves `.h` through the extension table above and lands on C. So the LSP side can already know a header is C++ while the grammar, the status-bar label, and every colour on screen still say C.

## Workaround that works today

Measured, same fixture, config:

```json
{
  "languages": {
    "cpp": { "extensions": ["cpp", "hpp", "cc", "hh", "cxx", "hxx", "h"] }
  }
}
```

gives:

```
 Trusted  Local  Ln 1, Col 1     Opened widget.h                           LF  ASCII  C++   LSP (off)   Palette: Ctrl+P
 3 │ [38;5;51mnamespace[38;5;231m ui [38;5;6m{
 4 │ [38;5;51mclass[38;5;231m [38;5;207mWidget[38;5;231m [38;5;2m{
```

It is global and unconditional, so it makes every `.h` C++ including in C projects — fine per-project, wrong as a default.

